station of the Dronecode project (https://github.com/mavlink/qgroundcontrol).
RotorLab Inc modified it in 2026; this notice was last updated on
2026-11-18. QGroundControl is Copyright (c) 2009-2024 QGroundControl
Project and its contributors, and is dual licensed under the Apache License
2.0 (LICENSE-APACHE) and the GNU General Public License v3 (LICENSE-GPL); see
COPYING.md. Upstream copyright and license notices are kept as they appear
upstream. RotorLab's changes are offered under the same two licenses, at your
choice.

RotorLab's release builds (the Windows installer, the Android APK and the
Linux AppImage) link Qt modules that are offered only under the GNU GPL v3
(Qt Charts and Qt Quick 3D) and embed ArduPilot parameter data generated
from GPLv3 source, so those builds are distributed under the GNU General
Public License v3.
Distributing a build under the Apache License 2.0 instead would need
commercial Qt licenses and the removal of the GPL-only parts.

The software is provided without warranty, as both licenses state.


WHAT ROTORLAB CHANGED

RotorLab added or changed, compared with QGroundControl (upstream commit
e0816c957602789200ae5ba0af45217f0f2f1db4):

- custom/: the RotorLab GC build (branding, Android manifest, CMake overrides)
  and RotorLab's own features. custom/src/CustomPlugin.cc,
  custom/src/CustomPlugin.h and custom/res/tak/SettingsPagesModel.qml are
  derived from upstream files (custom-example/src/CustomPlugin.* and
  src/UI/AppSettings/SettingsPagesModel.qml) and keep their upstream notices.
  RotorLab's features:
  - the 3D view of the plan in Plan view, with editing (custom/src/plan3d,
    custom/res/plan3d; Windows and Linux builds);
  - TAK / ATAK (custom/src/tak, custom/res/tak): publishing aircraft to a TAK
    server, commands from ATAK markers behind per-verb switches and a master
    arm, the command list, banner and command log, and TAK enrollment;
  - RotorLab Connector (custom/src/rotorlab, custom/res/rotorlab): flight
    filing to RotorLab, the station queue, the crew screen, the remote pilot
    in command log, checklists and missions from RotorLab;
  - Fleet Server connection (custom/src/fleet, custom/res/fleet);
  - license and Device Key storage (custom/src/license, custom/res/license,
    custom/src/rotorlab/Credential.*), including the check of RotorLab's
    signed offline activation record (custom/src/license/LicenseRecord.*,
    custom/src/license/Ed25519.*, a wrapper over the vendored Monocypher in
    custom/src/license/third_party/monocypher, and custom/license-pubkeys.txt),
    and network helpers (custom/src/net).
- src/: the responsive full-window settings layout (for example
  src/QmlControls/RLPageLayout.qml and the pages in src/UI/AppSettings), a
  per-user single-instance check (src/RunGuard.*), and smaller fixes.
- test/Custom/: unit tests for RotorLab's features.
- cmake/, CMakeLists.txt, android/, custom/android/, deploy/: build options,
  the Windows installer and version resource, the Linux AppImage packaging
  (cmake/CreateAppImage.cmake), installing the license files with the
  binaries, the release scripts deploy/rotorlab/release.ps1 and
  deploy/rotorlab/linux/, and the notice check deploy/rotorlab/check-notice.py.
- Documentation and notices: NOTICE, COPYING.md, licenses/, CHANGELOG.md
  (RotorLab section).


